<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Governance on Incredible Technology, Incredibly Simple</title><link>https://damianflynn.github.io/categories/governance/</link><description>Recent content in Governance on Incredible Technology, Incredibly Simple</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Oct 2019 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://damianflynn.github.io/categories/governance/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Installing Docker and Compose on Raspbian Buster</title><link>https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/installing-docker-and-compose-on-raspbian-buster/</link><pubDate>Tue, 01 Oct 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/installing-docker-and-compose-on-raspbian-buster/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Quickly update a new Raspberry Pi, which has an install of Raspbian Buster with Docker and Docker-compose.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class="relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px"&gt;
 &lt;div id="docker" class="absolute -top-28"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 Docker
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is simple, as the Docker team have done all the work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code-block highlight show-line-numbers my-2"&gt;
 &lt;details class="code-block-details" open&gt;
 &lt;summary class="code-block-title "&gt;
 &lt;span class="code-block-label"&gt;bash&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="code-block-toggle"&gt;&lt;span class="code-block-show"&gt;Show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="code-block-hide"&gt;Hide&lt;/span&gt; 2 lines&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="code-block-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button type="button" class="code-block-copy" data-code-target="codeblock-id-316f508ce637ffd096d16c1503bdef94-0" hidden&gt;Copy code&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;span class="code-block-chevron" aria-hidden="true"&gt;⌄&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/summary&gt;
 &lt;pre style="counter-reset: codeblock;" class="block"&gt;&lt;code
 id="codeblock-id-316f508ce637ffd096d16c1503bdef94-0"
 class="chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;curl -fsSL get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sh get-docker.sh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
 &lt;/details&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And, we can add our user to the Docker group so we do not need the &lt;code&gt;sudo&lt;/code&gt; every time. I am using the environment variable &lt;code&gt;$USER&lt;/code&gt;; which indicates who is logged in currently. In my case this is the user &lt;em&gt;pi&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>